From: Rhizomatica Mercury project
Subject: [PATCH] Cocoa: fall back to the software OpenGL renderer when no
 accelerated pixel format exists

On a GPU-less macOS environment (e.g. a QEMU/KVM VM guest with no accelerated
renderer), _glfwCreateContextNSGL() fails outright:

    NSGL: Failed to find a suitable pixel format

_glfwCreateContextNSGL() adds NSOpenGLPFAAccelerated as attribs[0], which
*requires* a hardware renderer. A CGLQueryRendererInfo() probe on such a guest
shows exactly one renderer, the Apple Software Renderer
(id & kCGLRendererIDMatchingMask == kCGLRendererGenericFloatID, accelerated=0,
window=1) — usable, but NSOpenGLPixelFormat never selects it because the
accelerated attribute rules it out.

If the accelerated pixel format is unavailable, retry once with attribs[0]
(NSOpenGLPFAAccelerated) dropped, so macOS can return the software renderer
instead of failing. Hardware stays strictly preferred: the accelerated attempt
runs first, so machines with a GPU never reach the fallback and behavior there
is unchanged.

Refs: glfw/glfw#2080, go-gl/glfw#335, fyne-io/fyne#2373

--- a/src/nsgl_context.m
+++ b/src/nsgl_context.m
@@ -313,6 +313,19 @@ GLFWbool _glfwCreateContextNSGL(_GLFWwindow* window,
         [[NSOpenGLPixelFormat alloc] initWithAttributes:attribs];
     if (window->context.nsgl.pixelFormat == nil)
     {
+        // Fall back to the software renderer on GPU-less systems (e.g. VM
+        // guests with no accelerated renderer). attribs[0] is always
+        // NSOpenGLPFAAccelerated (added at the top of this function); no pixel
+        // format can satisfy it without hardware acceleration. Retry once from
+        // attribs+1 so macOS returns its software (kCGLRendererGenericFloatID)
+        // renderer instead of failing. Hardware stays strictly preferred: the
+        // accelerated attempt runs first, so GPU machines never reach here.
+        assert(attribs[0] == NSOpenGLPFAAccelerated);
+        window->context.nsgl.pixelFormat =
+            [[NSOpenGLPixelFormat alloc] initWithAttributes:(attribs + 1)];
+    }
+    if (window->context.nsgl.pixelFormat == nil)
+    {
         _glfwInputError(GLFW_FORMAT_UNAVAILABLE,
                         "NSGL: Failed to find a suitable pixel format");
         return GLFW_FALSE;
